[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `run_all.sh` exists because **`cargo test` does not rebuild the `cdylib`**: the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m integration tests `dlopen` the `.so` instead of linking it, so cargo sees no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m dependency and happily leaves a stale library in `target/release/`. Running
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cargo test` alone can therefore "pass" against a library that does not contain
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m your latest edit. Always go through the script (or `cargo build --release`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m first).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both `.so` paths can be overridden with `C_SO_PATH` / `RUST_SO_PATH`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Test layout
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
